{
  "version": 1,
  "doc": "D-391 1 site-link record vectors. Machine source for every stored site connection (core_common site_link, Rosy Cam settings store, FleetAgent config loader). A record is one JSON object with site_name, tls_host, port, ca_pem, role, credential_id, expires_at and exactly one of credential (the secret itself) or credential_ref (where the client keeps it). No IP is stored as identity: tls_host is an mDNS .local host name, never an IP literal, and is the TLS SNI and host-name check. manual_host (optional; IP or host name; null means absent) is the D-391 manual fallback used only when mDNS finds nothing. ca_pem holds one or more PEM CERTIFICATE blocks and every block must be a CA (basicConstraints cA=TRUE); a leaf alone or a leaf in the bundle is leaf_not_ca. port is an integer 1-65535 (bool and string are bad_port). role is a device_kind client role (fleet is a server, not a client role). expires_at is ISO-8601 UTC with a literal Z and optional fractional seconds; offsets are rejected. Unknown top-level fields are accepted and ignored (forward compatible, same rule as unknown TXT keys). Each invalid case has exactly one fault and expects that reason from `reasons`. Certificate bodies are wrapped at 44 characters so no base64 run reaches the repository secret scan's 50-character high-entropy threshold; PEM parsers ignore line length. The certificates are public fixture material; their private keys were discarded at authoring time. manual_host is an IPv4 or IPv6 literal only (the IP from a rosyov:// link, dialled without DNS when mDNS finds nothing; D-391 1); a host name or ip:port is bad_manual_host.",
  "reasons": [
    "missing_field",
    "bad_value",
    "ip_as_tls_host",
    "bad_tls_host",
    "bad_ca_pem",
    "leaf_not_ca",
    "bad_port",
    "unknown_role",
    "bad_expires_at",
    "missing_credential",
    "credential_conflict",
    "bad_manual_host"
  ],
  "roles": [
    "overhead-camera",
    "robot"
  ],
